# AMD64 thunk export spec -- wldap32.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Boltgun imports this module STATICALLY and
# it had no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module
# (c000007b) and the whole image failed to load (c0000135).
#
# Boltgun imports it BY ORDINAL AND ONLY BY ORDINAL -- sixteen numbers, no
# names, which is exactly the class of request the ordinal work of 2026-08-17
# made answerable at all.  Measured, with the names Wine's own wldap32.spec
# gives those numbers:
#
#   143 ldap_init          46 ldap_unbind_s       211 ldap_set_option
#    60 ldap_simple_bind_s 50 ldap_search_s        41 ldap_msgfree
#    22 ldap_err2string   200 ldap_memfree         26 ldap_first_entry
#    27 ldap_next_entry    32 ldap_first_attribute 33 ldap_next_attribute
#    35 ldap_get_values_len 79 ldap_value_free_len 30 ldap_get_dn
#   301 ber_free
DLL wldap32.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# winldap.h is not in the oracle's default translation unit; without it every
# one of the 244 eligible exports was refused.  With it, 169 are emitted.
#
# The 75 still refused -- including ten of Boltgun's sixteen -- are NOT a
# shape this generator cannot describe.  They are the ANSI/Unicode pairs:
# winldap.h declares ldap_initA (line 535) and ldap_initW (536) and never the
# undecorated name, which it instead #defines through Wine's own A/W macro
# (`#define ldap_memfree WINELIB_NAME_AW(ldap_memfree)` and its ~120 siblings).
# The oracle looks up the export name the .spec publishes -- ldap_init -- and
# finds no declaration under it.  The same macro-rename hides all 27 exports
# of psapi.dll (see dlls/psapi/psapi.thunks), by a different macro and for a
# different reason, which is what makes it a class rather than a quirk: the
# oracle resolves an export NAME, and a header is entitled to declare that
# name's implementation under another one.  It is a gap in the signature
# oracle, not in this module, and ppc64le/corpus/CATALOG.md records it as
# such rather than papering over it here.  Each of the ten keeps its ordinal
# as a named sentinel, so a guest that CALLS one faults by name; Boltgun
# imports them and, so far, calls none.
PROBE-EXTRA   winldap.h
